{
  "_comment": [
    "Spike fixture, not a canonical ADR-0001 document. Adaptations, all of them",
    "presentation-only and all of them additive:",
    "  1. This top-level '_comment' key and the per-block '_comment' keys are NOT",
    "     part of the ADR-0001 envelope or the {type,id,config,slots} node shape.",
    "     A strict StatifierBlocks.Document.from_json/1 would need them stripped.",
    "     They exist so the spike's fixtures document themselves without a README.",
    "  2. Written pretty-printed with keys in reading order (type, id, type_version,",
    "     config, slots). ADR-0001 decision 8's canonical form is byte-sorted and",
    "     whitespace-free; that form is the encoder's output, not what a human edits.",
    "  3. Empty slots are omitted and leaf blocks carry no 'slots' key, which DOES",
    "     follow decision 8.",
    "  4. No floats anywhere (decision 6): money is integer minor units, durations",
    "     are ISO-8601 strings.",
    "Block types: the seven core.* types are real (StatifierBlocks.Core). The",
    "eighth, core.invoke, is NOT - it is the proposed descriptor in",
    "spike/js/proposed-core.js, registered beside the real ones so the spike can",
    "show what a core type with an outcome slot would look like. Every",
    "myapp.* type is a demo palette entry the spike registers; three of them exist",
    "because the core set has no equivalent - see the '_comment' on each first use.",
    "The single deliberately-unresolvable type is myapp.legacy_check (blk_cp_legacy).",
    "Both failure idioms are present on purpose, so one document can be read for",
    "the comparison: idiom A is core.invoke's on_error SLOT (blk_cp_authorize with",
    "a park-and-notify sequence, blk_cp_capture with a lone park), and idiom B is",
    "the predicate branch (blk_cp_capture_retry), which is left exactly as it was.",
    "Shape: 45 blocks, maximum nesting depth 7 (root = depth 1).",
    "Every datamodel path named in a 'cond' resolves in ../datamodel.json."
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "bdoc_cp_demo",
  "revision": 42,
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Card processing",
    "description": "Intake, validation, a three-lane authorization group with interrupts, an outcome branch with capture retry and manual review, and a receipt tail. The authorize and capture calls carry on_error subtrees, so the slot idiom and the retry-predicate idiom can be read side by side.",
    "domain": "card-processing"
  },
  "root": {
    "type": "core.sequence",
    "id": "blk_cp_root",
    "type_version": 1,
    "slots": {
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "myapp.intake",
          "id": "blk_cp_intake",
          "type_version": 1,
          "config": {
            "invoke_type": "myapp:intake",
            "label": "Take the payment request"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "core.branch",
          "id": "blk_cp_validation",
          "type_version": 1,
          "config": {
            "arms": [
              {
                "slot": "arm_valid",
                "cond": "validation.passed AND amount_cents > 0 AND card.active"
              }
            ]
          },
          "slots": {
            "arm_valid": [
              {
                "_comment": "Depth 3. The authorization group: body holds the lanes and the authorize call, interrupts hold two guarded rules.",
                "type": "core.group",
                "id": "blk_cp_authz",
                "type_version": 1,
                "slots": {
                  "body": [
                    {
                      "type": "core.parallel",
                      "id": "blk_cp_lanes",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "lanes": ["fraud_review", "balance_check", "three_ds"]
                      },
                      "slots": {
                        "lane_fraud_review": [
                          {
                            "_comment": "Depth 5. A nested group inside a lane: its own body, its own interrupt rail.",
                            "type": "core.group",
                            "id": "blk_cp_fraud",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "slots": {
                              "body": [
                                {
                                  "type": "myapp.risk_rating",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_risk_rating",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "invoke_type": "myapp:risk_rating",
                                    "label": "Rate the transaction"
                                  }
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "core.wait",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_fraud_wait",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "duration": "PT2M"
                                  }
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "core.branch",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_risk_branch",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "arms": [
                                      {
                                        "slot": "arm_high_risk",
                                        "cond": "risk_rating >= 70 OR fraud.verdict == 'review'"
                                      },
                                      {
                                        "slot": "arm_low_risk",
                                        "cond": "risk_rating < 40 AND customer.verified"
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "slots": {
                                    "arm_high_risk": [
                                      {
                                        "type": "myapp.manual_flag",
                                        "id": "blk_cp_manual_flag",
                                        "type_version": 1,
                                        "config": {
                                          "invoke_type": "myapp:manual_flag",
                                          "label": "Flag for a human"
                                        }
                                      }
                                    ],
                                    "arm_low_risk": [
                                      {
                                        "_comment": "THE UNRESOLVABLE BLOCK (ADR-0005 decision 12). No palette in the spike registers myapp.legacy_check, so it must render with unavailable chrome, a :block finding, its config read-only as JSON, and its bytes preserved on save. It is deliberately at depth 7 so the case is exercised deep in the tree rather than at the top.",
                                        "type": "myapp.legacy_check",
                                        "id": "blk_cp_legacy",
                                        "type_version": 3,
                                        "config": {
                                          "ruleset": "velocity-v2",
                                          "window": "PT24H",
                                          "thresholds": {
                                            "count": 5,
                                            "amount_cents": 250000
                                          }
                                        }
                                      }
                                    ],
                                    "otherwise": [
                                      {
                                        "type": "myapp.notify",
                                        "id": "blk_cp_risk_notify",
                                        "type_version": 1,
                                        "config": {
                                          "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                                          "template": "risk_indeterminate",
                                          "label": "Tell ops the rating was inconclusive"
                                        }
                                      }
                                    ]
                                  }
                                }
                              ],
                              "interrupts": [
                                {
                                  "type": "core.on_event",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_fraud_abort",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "event": "fraud.aborted",
                                    "outcome": "abandon"
                                  }
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ],
                        "lane_balance_check": [
                          {
                            "type": "myapp.balance_check",
                            "id": "blk_cp_balance",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "config": {
                              "invoke_type": "myapp:balance_check",
                              "label": "Check the available balance"
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "core.wait",
                            "id": "blk_cp_balance_wait",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "config": {
                              "duration": "PT30S"
                            }
                          }
                        ],
                        "lane_three_ds": [
                          {
                            "type": "myapp.three_ds_challenge",
                            "id": "blk_cp_three_ds",
                            "type_version": 2,
                            "config": {
                              "invoke_type": "myapp:three_ds",
                              "label": "Send the cardholder a challenge"
                            }
                          },
                          {
                            "_comment": "The on-event-plus-timeout idiom: a group whose whole body is a wait, with the completion event on its interrupt rail. The wait is the timeout; the event is the happy path.",
                            "type": "core.group",
                            "id": "blk_cp_three_ds_group",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "slots": {
                              "body": [
                                {
                                  "type": "core.wait",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_three_ds_wait",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "duration": "PT10M"
                                  }
                                }
                              ],
                              "interrupts": [
                                {
                                  "type": "core.on_event",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_three_ds_done",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "event": "card.three_ds_completed",
                                    "outcome": "resume"
                                  }
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "_comment": "FAILURE IDIOM A, and the PROPOSED type core.invoke (spike/js/proposed-core.js) - not a shipped core type. The error path is a SLOT the block type declares (umbrella D13, 2026-08-28), so the failure edge is a parent/slot/child relationship like every other edge and the connector stays rendered rather than authored. Idiom B is blk_cp_capture_retry further down: the same kind of failure handled by a predicate the author writes. Three things the rework gave up, all Phase-B findings and none of them decided here: (1) core.invoke declares no 'label' field, so the 'label' below is stored data the canvas titles the card from while the inspector form cannot edit it - every myapp.* step declares one and the proposed core type does not; (2) myapp.authorize's 'timeout' key has no core.invoke equivalent, so it is dropped rather than carried as undeclared config - the authorization timeout already lives on this group's interrupt rail as blk_cp_authz_timeout, which is where a timeout belongs; (3) type_version drops from 2 to 1, because core.invoke's currentVersion is 1 and a stored version above the descriptor's is a hard block_type_too_new refusal.",
                      "type": "core.invoke",
                      "id": "blk_cp_authorize",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "invoke_type": "myapp:authorize",
                        "assign_to": "authorization",
                        "params": "amount=amount_cents\ncurrency=currency\ncustomer=customer.id",
                        "label": "Authorize the card"
                      },
                      "slots": {
                        "on_error": [
                          {
                            "_comment": "Depth 5. The on_error slot is zero_or_one, so a failure path of more than one step needs a container - a sequence here, and the two steps sit at depth 6.",
                            "type": "core.sequence",
                            "id": "blk_cp_authz_error",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "slots": {
                              "body": [
                                {
                                  "type": "myapp.park",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_authz_park",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "invoke_type": "myapp:park",
                                    "queue": "authorization_review",
                                    "label": "Queue it for review"
                                  }
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "myapp.notify",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_authz_error_notify",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                                    "template": "authorization_failed",
                                    "label": "Tell ops the authorization failed"
                                  }
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "interrupts": [
                    {
                      "_comment": "Demo type #1. core.on_event carries only event + outcome; it has no condition. A conditioned interrupt rule is what the spike needs to render a guard on an exit edge, so the demo palette adds myapp.guarded_on_event = core.on_event plus a 'cond'. If the spike proves the affordance is worth it, that is an ADR-0002 amendment to propose, not something this fixture decides.",
                      "type": "myapp.guarded_on_event",
                      "id": "blk_cp_cancelled",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "event": "customer.cancelled",
                        "cond": "event.customer_cancelled.reason == 'customer_request' AND auth.captured == false",
                        "outcome": "abandon"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "_comment": "Demo type #2. The PT15M authorization timeout. No core type expresses 'interrupt this group after a duration'; core.wait is a step inside a body, not a rule on an interrupt rail. myapp.timeout_rule = an 'after' duration plus an optional guard.",
                      "type": "myapp.timeout_rule",
                      "id": "blk_cp_authz_timeout",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "after": "PT15M",
                        "cond": "three_ds.completed == false OR fraud.cleared == false",
                        "outcome": "abandon"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "otherwise": [
              {
                "type": "myapp.notify",
                "id": "blk_cp_validation_fail",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                  "template": "validation_failed",
                  "label": "Tell the customer what was wrong"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "core.branch",
          "id": "blk_cp_outcome",
          "type_version": 1,
          "config": {
            "arms": [
              {
                "slot": "arm_approved",
                "cond": "auth.approved AND fraud.cleared AND balance.available_cents >= amount_cents"
              },
              {
                "slot": "arm_declined",
                "cond": "fraud.verdict == 'decline' OR balance.available_cents < amount_cents"
              },
              {
                "slot": "arm_manual_review",
                "cond": "fraud.verdict == 'review' AND limits.manual_review_backlog < 50"
              }
            ]
          },
          "slots": {
            "arm_approved": [
              {
                "type": "core.group",
                "id": "blk_cp_capture_group",
                "type_version": 1,
                "slots": {
                  "body": [
                    {
                      "_comment": "FAILURE IDIOM A in its minimal shape: the on_error slot holding one leaf step rather than a container. Idiom B sits directly below it, and this pair is the comparison the document exists to make. The predicate branch can only see failures the datamodel records (auth.captured == false, capture_attempts < 3); the on_error slot catches the ones it cannot, including the call never answering at all. Neither idiom subsumes the other, which is why both are kept here rather than one replacing the other. 'amount_key' is gone: params carries the same fact as a name=path pair, which is what core.invoke declares.",
                      "type": "core.invoke",
                      "id": "blk_cp_capture",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "invoke_type": "myapp:capture",
                        "params": "amount=amount_cents\nauth_code=auth.code",
                        "label": "Capture the funds"
                      },
                      "slots": {
                        "on_error": [
                          {
                            "type": "myapp.park",
                            "id": "blk_cp_capture_park",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "config": {
                              "invoke_type": "myapp:park",
                              "queue": "capture_reconciliation",
                              "label": "Park it for reconciliation"
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "_comment": "FAILURE IDIOM B, unchanged from before the rework and deliberately so: the retry idiom is a one-armed branch whose arm is a wait-then-repeat sequence, and its guard is an ordinary condition the author wrote. Read it beside the on_error slot above - same failure, one edge declared by the block type and one edge derived from the datamodel.",
                      "type": "core.branch",
                      "id": "blk_cp_capture_retry",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "arms": [
                          {
                            "slot": "arm_retry",
                            "cond": "auth.captured == false AND capture_attempts < 3"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "slots": {
                        "arm_retry": [
                          {
                            "type": "core.sequence",
                            "id": "blk_cp_retry_seq",
                            "type_version": 1,
                            "slots": {
                              "body": [
                                {
                                  "type": "core.wait",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_retry_wait",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "duration": "PT1M"
                                  }
                                },
                                {
                                  "_comment": "Left on the host type on purpose, where the first capture moved to core.invoke. Two reasons, both about what the document has to keep proving: the retry idiom reads honestly only if the block inside it is the block a host writes today, and myapp.capture is the one type in the palette pointing at its own accent token (--sb-accent-myapp-capture, overridden in css/themes/host-brand.css), so this is the last instance of the accent-layering demo on the canvas. A pass that converted it too would delete both without saying so.",
                                  "type": "myapp.capture",
                                  "id": "blk_cp_capture_retry_call",
                                  "type_version": 1,
                                  "config": {
                                    "invoke_type": "myapp:capture",
                                    "amount_key": "amount_cents",
                                    "retries": 3,
                                    "label": "Try the capture again"
                                  }
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "interrupts": [
                    {
                      "type": "core.on_event",
                      "id": "blk_cp_capture_cancel",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "event": "capture.reversed",
                        "outcome": "abandon"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "arm_declined": [
              {
                "type": "myapp.notify",
                "id": "blk_cp_decline_notify",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                  "template": "payment_declined",
                  "label": "Tell the customer it was declined"
                }
              }
            ],
            "arm_manual_review": [
              {
                "_comment": "The park / needs-attention idiom inside a resumable group with deep history: the work parks, a human resolves it days later, and re-entry lands back where it stopped.",
                "type": "core.resumable_group",
                "id": "blk_cp_manual",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "history": "deep"
                },
                "slots": {
                  "body": [
                    {
                      "type": "myapp.park",
                      "id": "blk_cp_park",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "invoke_type": "myapp:park",
                        "queue": "manual_review",
                        "label": "Park it for a reviewer"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "core.wait",
                      "id": "blk_cp_manual_wait",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "duration": "P2D"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "myapp.resolve_review",
                      "id": "blk_cp_resolve",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "invoke_type": "myapp:resolve_review",
                        "label": "Apply the reviewer's decision"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "interrupts": [
                    {
                      "type": "myapp.guarded_on_event",
                      "id": "blk_cp_manual_resolved",
                      "type_version": 1,
                      "config": {
                        "event": "review.resolved",
                        "cond": "event.review_resolved.decision == 'approve' AND review.parked",
                        "outcome": "resume"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "otherwise": [
              {
                "type": "myapp.notify",
                "id": "blk_cp_outcome_fallback",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                  "template": "outcome_indeterminate",
                  "label": "Tell ops no outcome arm matched"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "core.sequence",
          "id": "blk_cp_tail",
          "type_version": 1,
          "slots": {
            "body": [
              {
                "type": "myapp.receipt",
                "id": "blk_cp_receipt",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "invoke_type": "myapp:receipt",
                  "label": "Build the receipt"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "myapp.notify",
                "id": "blk_cp_final_notify",
                "type_version": 1,
                "config": {
                  "invoke_type": "myapp:notify",
                  "template": "receipt_ready",
                  "label": "Send the receipt"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
